<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan sugar output reaches 1.979 million tonnes.</title>
<headline>Pakistan sugar output reaches 1.979 million tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Sugar Mills Association said on Saturday sugar production had reached 1.979 million tonnes by March 15 compared to 2.185 million tonnes at the same time a year ago.</p>
<p>It said mills aimed to produce 2.4 million tonnes in 1996/97, compared to 2.47 million in 1995/96 and 3.0 million in 1994/95. Dealers bought 910,130 tonnes, or 45.97 percent, of the production and the remaining 1.069 million tonnes was at the mills.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
